== ψ Current Density and the Poynting Identity ==

The spatial ψ current density vector is:

:<math>
\mathbf{J}_\psi = (J^1_\psi, J^2_\psi, J^3_\psi) = -\nabla\psi\cdot\partial_t\psi = -(\partial_t\psi)\nabla\psi
</math>

This is identical to the ψ Poynting vector derived on the [[Psionics]] page:

:<math>
\vec{S}_\psi = -\partial_t\psi\,\nabla\psi = \mathbf{J}_\psi
</math>

'''The ψ current density and the ψ energy flux are the same object.''' This unification — analogous to the fact that in electromagnetism the energy flux and the momentum density of the field are related — has an immediate engineering implication: a device that guides ψ energy flow (a [[ψ Waveguide]]) is simultaneously guiding ψ charge flow. There is no separate "ψ charge conduit" distinct from a ψ energy conduit.

