== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

The following applications assume the ψ field hypothesis is experimentally confirmed. They are Track B content — engineering predictions, not established physics.

=== Biological ψ Charge Rate ===

From the [[Psionics]] page, the biological source term is:

:<math>J_\psi^{\rm (src)}(x,t) \propto \int f\bigl(u(x',t)\bigr)\,d^3x'</math>

where <math>f(u)</math> is the neural firing rate from the Wilson–Cowan model. The total ψ charge generation rate by an operator is therefore:

:<math>\frac{dQ_\psi^{\rm (bio)}}{dt} = \int J_\psi^{\rm (src)}\,d^3x \propto \int\!\!\int f(u)\,d^3x'\,d^3x</math>

The [[HRV as ψ Proxy]] page argues that RMSSD coherence correlates with the ''coherent'' component of <math>f(u)</math> — the part that contributes constructively to <math>Q_\psi</math> rather than canceling due to phase incoherence across cortical columns. This is the biological coupling that the [[HRV-Gated Drive]] tracks.

=== ψ Charge Budget for the Psi Stabilizer ===

At steady state during Anchor mode, the [[Psi Stabilizer]] maintains a fixed <math>Q_\psi</math> inside the resonant shell. The continuity equation at steady state gives:

:<math>0 = J_\psi^{\rm (device)} + J_\psi^{\rm (bio)} - \frac{Q_\psi}{\tau_\psi}</math>

where <math>\tau_\psi = Q_\psi / (\text{ψ charge dissipation rate})</math> is the ψ charge lifetime in the shell (related to <math>Q_\psi</math> quality factor from [[ψ Quality Factor]]). The [[Anchor Controller]] regulates <math>J_\psi^{\rm (device)}</math> to maintain the balance. The Mk2.0 HRV-gated mode estimates <math>J_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math> from RMSSD and adjusts <math>J_\psi^{\rm (device)}</math> accordingly.

